Notes:

Linked List: a data structure that stores information in separate objects called nodes
    - nodes are connected using pointers, last node points to nullptr (where travesal ends)
        - Data: information stored in the node
        - Pointer: An address that tells the program where the next node is located

Circular Linked List: similar to linked list but instead the last node points back to the first node

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

