Monopoly Board:

addProperty functon is the same as insertAtEnd, builds the circular board

printProperties walks the circle once and prints every property's name, cost, and owner

searchProperty walks the circle looking for a matching name. Returns a pointer to the node(or nullptr if not found)

removeProperty: more complex because it has to handle
-empty list
-only one node
-deleting the head
-deleing a node in the middle/end
It returns true if it successfully removed the property

summary of all paths:

if list is empty: do nothing : returns false
if only one node + name matches : delete it, set head = nullptr : returns true
if only one node + name does not match : do nothing : returns flase
if multiple nodes + delete head : find tail, rewire, move head, and delete : return true
if multiple nodes + delete middle/end : skip over the node and delete it : returns true
if name not found : do nothing : returns false


